# Consent and intercept rules

## Consent modes (`ConsentMode`)

| Mode | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| `always` | Auto-redirect via support (sync storage); use `quiet=1` on `/support` |
| `session` | Legacy auto until browser session ends (same quiet redirects). New „Ja, diesmal“ does **not** set this |
| `snoozed` | „Erstmal nicht“ — 3 days (`CONSENT_SNOOZE_MS`); click + landing both **ignore** (no dialog) |
| `never` | Never ask / never redirect; click + landing both **ignore** |
| `unset` | Show opt-in dialog |

### Opt-in dialog actions

| Button | Behavior |
|--------|----------|
| Ja, immer | `setConsentAlways` → `/support` (brief thank-you, no `quiet`) |
| Ja, diesmal | **True one-shot**: no consent storage → `/support` once; later clicks ask again |
| Erstmal nicht | `setConsentSnooze` → untagged dest |
| Nie | `setConsentNever` → untagged dest |
| Esc / backdrop | No storage change → untagged dest (do not cancel navigation) |

## Skip intercept when

1. Destination already has a non-empty affiliate param (`hasExistingAffiliateTag`)
2. Already browsing the **same partner host** (in-shop clicks / product→product)
3. Coming back from `/support` (thank-you → shop)
4. URL is the support page itself

## Amazon tagging (website only)

- Product paths `/dp/ASIN` or `/gp/product/ASIN`: add `?tag=` **and** `/ref=nosim`
- All other Amazon URLs: `?tag=` **only** — never append `/ref=nosim` (soft-404 on cart/wishlist/etc.)
